# Backend modules

## Feature skeleton

```
<feature>/
  <feature>.ts           # createX(deps) — deep core
  <feature>.types.ts     # ports + public types
  index.ts               # composition only
  <feature>.router.ts    # Zod → core → map errors
  <feature>.repository.ts
  *.test.ts              # test through the interface
```

Watch pipeline: keep under `title/watch/` with its own entry — don’t scatter new watch files at `title/` root.

## Import DAG (down only)

```
router / worker
  → feature core (via createX)
    → adapters (db/*, qbittorrent, storage, tracker)
      → infra (http, env)
```

**Forbidden**

- Feature A imports Feature B implementation (repos, internals)
- Router contains business logic
- Infra (proxy agent, generic fetch) living under `torrent/` — use `http/`
- `*.repository` importing Catalog (or any feature core) for types — types stay with the data owner

**Allowed**

- `index.ts` wires adapters + settings ports into `createX`
- Home reads feed/watch data via ports or read-model helpers, not title repositories
- Catalog owns search orchestration; tRPC `torrent.*` may alias into Catalog

## Naming

- Prefer `<entity>.<role>.ts` (`title.repository.ts`, `torrent.router.ts`)
- Folder `qbittorent` is legacy spelling — when renaming, use `qbittorrent` only
